@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@*
    #251 item 1 · THE STORY PLATE, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    Moved out of Map.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block that was in
    the page, character for character. Every page member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME NAME (the
    fields keep their underscore, the methods come across as delegates), which is what lets the markup move
    without a rewrite and lets the suite's source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as before.

    The `@if` that opens it stays in Map.razor, and so does the paragraph above it about WHERE it renders:
    #994 put this plate at the FOOT of .map-flowcolumn, and that is the host's own geometry — the reason it
    lands on the pixels it lands on is the flow, not this file. What moved here is the plate's own note and
    the plate's own markup.

    IHandleEvent repeats the page's own override (Map.Sim.cs) — without it Blazor would put an automatic
    re-render back on every event in here, which the page turns off because the HUD's refresh belongs to
    OnTick's 200 ms throttle. The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules: `.story-plate` and its
    `story-plate-in` keyframes stay together in Pages/Map.razor.css, where #1109 deliberately kept them
    (an animation cut off from its keyframes is that PR's first named trap), so the cascade does not move.

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block used to sit inside `@if (…) { … }`,
    which is a Razor CODE block, and a code block is where its first statements are legal — this one
    OPENS with a statement (`var flashCopy = …`). The braces put the moved lines back in the context they
    were written in; they are outside the fences, so what the source guards read is still exactly the
    lines that were in the page.
*@
@* ── THE PAGE'S OWN NOTE ON THIS SURFACE, moved here with it (#251 item 1) and not touched by a
   word: it is the paragraph that stood above this block in Map.razor. It sits ABOVE the fence, not
   inside it, so that a source guard slicing the block by text goes on reading markup and not prose.
   ── *@
        @* The plate: same picture, same words, no keyboard stolen and no world stopped. The PANEL is still not
           clickable — a thing you must dismiss is a thing that blocked you — but #992 gives it the one control
           the owner's ruling asks of every surface in this file: "there should not be a pop-up that cannot be
           closed or minimized" (owner ruling 2026-08-24). The ✕ re-enables its own pointer-events and nothing
           else does, so the plate goes on passing every other click through to the room behind it. The great
           port's own plate is what made the case: ArrivalTube.Title(GreatPort) is "🛬 THE LONG WALK IN", it
           carries the longest of the three captions, and it lands bottom-left across the captain's-remote
           button for the whole of StoryBeats.PlateSeconds. *@

@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from Map.razor ───────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
            var flashCopy = StoryBeatCopy(flash.Beat, flash.Subject);
            @* #997 · the plate is an OverlayShell in its BARE frame: no head row, no body wrapper, and the
               way out is the LAST child — which is exactly the geometry #996 measured and #992 gave it. The
               plate is one flex row of [art][words][✕], so the shell puts nothing between them. *@
            <OverlayShell class="story-plate" aria-live="polite"
                          Frame="OverlayFrame.Bare" Dismiss="OverlayDismiss.Close"
                          DismissClass="story-plate-close" DismissFace="✕" DismissLabel="Close"
                          DismissTitle="Take it down now — it would go on its own in a few seconds"
                          OnClose="() => Dismiss(CloseStoryPlate)">
                @if (flashCopy.Art is { Length: > 0 })
                {
                    <img class="story-plate-art" src="@flashCopy.Art" alt=""
                         onerror="this.style.display='none'" />
                }
                <div class="story-plate-words">
                    <div class="story-plate-title">@flashCopy.Title</div>
                    <div class="story-plate-caption">@flashCopy.Caption</div>
                </div>
            </OverlayShell>
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}
